<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 340 0 R
/E (The discussions emphasized that while advanced models and techniques are important, real-world systems must prioritize stability, robustness, and consistency over complexity. It was noted that computer vision systems commonly face challenges such as variations in lighting conditions, occlusion between individuals, similar appearances among different people, and inconsistent detections across frames. To address these issues, it was suggested that systems should not rely on a single model, but instead combine multiple components such as detection, tracking, and identity matching to improve overall reliability.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
776 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
