>>
endobj
996 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (This project attempts to solve one operational issue in particular, that is, who is in each frame across a network of cameras, where are they, and is the person currently visible on Camera 3 the same person who was seen on Camera 1 earlier? To solve this problem, there are needed four different technical tools that solve four specific sub-questions.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
997 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (Person Detection)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
998 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (The very first part in the pipeline is the detection of every single person in every single frame. We use one of the best models that exists for such purposes, YOLOv11m, that operates on an input image resolution of 1280 px. )
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
999 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (Why exactly this resolution is chosen? Because persons located far away, partially occluded, or in low-confidence areas in the frame are detectable only at such resolution; otherwise, they would not be detected at all. Moreover, our model outputs only detections of persons; also, two confidence mechanisms are utilized here.)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1000 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (Within-Camera Tracking)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1001 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (After people have been successfully detected in a frame, we need to assign an identity to each individual and track this identity across multiple frames in the future. Such task is accomplished through the utilization of two different )
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1002 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (tools at once which are Kalman Filter and the Hungarian Algorithm. In )
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1003 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (short, we use the Kalman Filter to predict future positions of every tracked person according to their last location, speed, and change in size;  then, we apply the Hungarian Algorithm to match new detections to these predicted points in space. ..)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1004 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 357 0 R
/E (Cross-Camera Re-Identification)
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
